{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 2 'no-persist|sealed checkout.*review|checkout selado.*review' POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md-425-- `record-deployment` / `record-incident` / `dora-metrics` / `adoption-metrics` — ingerem eventos de entrega schema v2 sem identidade individual e calculam métricas para um ambiente de produção explícito (`--environment`, padrão `production`). Deployments exigem `--deployment-kind planned|rework`; incidentes exigem ambiente; recovery inclui apenas incidentes resolvidos com `--caused-by-deployment`. `adoption-metrics` agrega taxas de especificações, roadmaps e validação de ciclo de vida.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md-426-- `stacks [--path dir] [--json]` — inspeção de catálogo read-only e offline (spec pose-stack-catalog-expansion). Casa entradas de diretório contra o catálogo mantido de perfis (Node.js, Go, Rust, Java, **Python** — poetry/pipenv/pip/setuptools/pep517 — e **.NET**), reportando por perfil: manager, marker, `winner`/`shadowed` (múltiplos managers presentes resolvem por prioridade declarada), `confidence` (`medium` sob conflito) e se a ferramenta nativa pré-requisito está no `PATH` — via `exec.LookPath`, nunca executando um arquivo do projeto. Markers detectados alimentam `discoverValidationModules`/`pose init --wizard` do mesmo jeito que Node/Go/Rust/Java já fazem; os checks propriamente ditos rodam pelas stacks `python`/`dotnet` da [`validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json). A prioridade de manager Python é expressa com `when.fileNotExistsAny` (pular quando existir qualquer lockfile/marker de prioridade maior) ao lado dos predicados `fileExists`/`fileNotExists` já existentes.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:427:- `assess discover|integrate|tech-debt|stale|request|snapshot` — motores nativos de assessment para LOC, marcadores de débito técnico, estruturas de componentes, checagens de integridade de contrato entre módulos e ciclo de vida de reavaliação de capabilities. `discover`, `integrate` e `tech-debt` aceitam `--no-persist` para imprimir o resultado sem gravar `.pose/assessments/` nem `.pose/state/`; no checkout selado de uma review delegada (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`) eles nunca gravam, `init`, `snapshot` e `request` recusam, e o plano de review os roda com `--no-persist`, para que um revisor que roda um assessment planejado não derrube o próprio run.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md-428-- `doctor [--fix]` — diagnósticos de ambiente, dependências, runtime nativo e saúde da instância POSE, além de governança que só falharia mais adiante: `review.evidence-vocabulary` (um profile selecionado exige uma classe que nenhum check pode emitir), `validate.class-producers` (um critério aceita apenas classes que nenhum check registrado produz), `validate.evidence-class-coverage` (checks sem `evidenceClass`), `review.profile-schema`, `review.contract-adoption`, `review.scope-change-set` e `<policy>.policy-keys` para nove políticas (chaves que o motor não lê, ou seja, uma configuração com erro de digitação que silenciosamente não faz nada).\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md-429-- `knowledge-housekeeping` / `reports-housekeeping` / `events-housekeeping` — manutenção idempotente (listar/arquivar/expurgar). Mutações exigem `--apply`. O housekeeping de reports **nunca toca em `history/`**: o JSONL é a fonte de verdade para `recurrence-check` e comparações temporais de `report`. Defaults: stale = 120d, purga de arquivo = 365d.\n--\nPOSE.md-421-- `record-deployment` / `record-incident` / `dora-metrics` / `adoption-metrics` — ingest identity-free schema-v2 delivery events and calculate metrics for explicit production environments (`--environment`, default `production`). Deployments require `--deployment-kind planned|rework`; incidents require an environment; recovery includes only resolved `--caused-by-deployment` incidents. `adoption-metrics` aggregates specifications, roadmaps, and validation lifecycle rates.\nPOSE.md-422-- `stacks [--path dir] [--json]` — read-only, offline catalog inspection (spec pose-stack-catalog-expansion). Matches directory entries against the maintained profile catalog (Node.js, Go, Rust, Java, **Python** — poetry/pipenv/pip/setuptools/pep517 — and **.NET**), reporting per profile: manager, marker, `winner`/`shadowed` (multiple managers present resolve by declared priority), `confidence` (`medium` under conflict), and whether the prerequisite native tool is on `PATH` — via `exec.LookPath`, never by executing a project file. Detected markers feed `discoverValidationModules`/`pose init --wizard` the same way Node/Go/Rust/Java already do; the actual checks run through [`validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json) `python`/`dotnet` stacks. Python manager priority is expressed with `when.fileNotExistsAny` (skip when any higher-priority lockfile/marker exists) alongside the existing `fileExists`/`fileNotExists` predicates.\nPOSE.md:423:- `assess discover|integrate|tech-debt|stale|request|snapshot` — native assessment engines for LOC, technical debt markers, component structures, inter-module contract integrity checks, and capability mechanism reassessment lifecycle. `discover`, `integrate` and `tech-debt` take `--no-persist` to print their result without writing `.pose/assessments/` or `.pose/state/`; in the sealed checkout of a delegated review (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`) they never persist, `init`, `snapshot` and `request` refuse, and the review plan runs them with `--no-persist`, so a reviewer running a planned assessment does not fail its own run.\nPOSE.md-424-- `doctor [--fix]` — environment, dependency, native runtime, and POSE instance health diagnostics, plus governance that would otherwise fail only downstream: `review.evidence-vocabulary` (a selected profile demands a class no check may emit), `validate.class-producers` (a criterion accepts only classes no registered check produces), `validate.evidence-class-coverage` (checks with no `evidenceClass`), `review.profile-schema`, `review.contract-adoption`, `review.scope-change-set`, and `<policy>.policy-keys` for nine policies (keys the engine does not read, i.e. a misspelled setting that silently does nothing).\nPOSE.md-425-- `knowledge-housekeeping` / `reports-housekeeping` / `events-housekeeping` — idempotent maintenance (list/archive/purge). Mutations require `--apply`. Reports housekeeping **never touches `history/`**: the JSONL is the source of truth for `recurrence-check` and `report`'s temporal comparisons. Defaults: stale = 120d, archive purge = 365d.\n--\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md-421-- `record-deployment` / `record-incident` / `dora-metrics` / `adoption-metrics` — ingest identity-free schema-v2 delivery events and calculate metrics for explicit production environments (`--environment`, default `production`). Deployments require `--deployment-kind planned|rework`; incidents require an environment; recovery includes only resolved `--caused-by-deployment` incidents. `adoption-metrics` aggregates specifications, roadmaps, and validation lifecycle rates.\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md-422-- `stacks [--path dir] [--json]` — read-only, offline catalog inspection (spec pose-stack-catalog-expansion). Matches directory entries against the maintained profile catalog (Node.js, Go, Rust, Java, **Python** — poetry/pipenv/pip/setuptools/pep517 — and **.NET**), reporting per profile: manager, marker, `winner`/`shadowed` (multiple managers present resolve by declared priority), `confidence` (`medium` under conflict), and whether the prerequisite native tool is on `PATH` — via `exec.LookPath`, never by executing a project file. Detected markers feed `discov