{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The legacy assessment runs changed eight tracked `.pose/assessments` and `.pose/state` files. I won’t restore or edit them because the brief forbids repository changes; that means this run cannot be represented as a clean verified review. I’m doing the requested read-only draft preflight now and will report its result and the affected paths plainly."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go\",\n      \"line\": 658,\n      \"summary\": \"GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown writes .pose/assessments/<slug>.md without refuseSealedAssessmentWrite, so a Store caller can still mutate the sealed checkout despite the guards on SaveComponentState and the other assessment writers.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Verified review_dispatch.go appends POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT for the checkout and IsSealedCheckout resolves and compares the paths. L1 remains an accepted limitation: a reviewer process that clears the variable can write, with the dispatch tree comparison detecting the mutation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds no shared mutable state or asynchronous lifecycle. The no-persist paths skip publication; the focused Assess and ReviewPlanRunsAssessments Go tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sealed CLI write commands return a refusal, while Store assessment writes use the typed ErrSealedAssessmentWrite error. Focused CLI and pose package tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays within the pose-mcp assessment CLI and Store boundary; sealed integration evidence covers delegated review checkout handling.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI emits a persistence hint on stderr and direct Store callers receive a typed error with a remediation hint.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The three flags are additive; persisting paths remain the default outside a sealed checkout, JSON output keeps the same result shape, and no stored record schema changes.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"R1/R2 address persisted assessment files as the cause of sealed-run failures; D1'\"'s CLI skip plus Store guard is the smallest direct backstop, and D2 makes planned commands safe when copied. The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there are no delta mappings.\\\",\\\"mappings\\\":[]},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared the English and pt-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies with the CLI behavior and help entries; they describe --no-persist, sealed checkout behavior, refusal commands, and planned flags consistently.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The refusal paths explain why writes are blocked and the Store error names --no-persist. The focused tests passed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Changes are confined to the assessment CLI and Store writers, review plan, help, and the specified manuals/scaffold copies. The one omitted writer guard is recorded as N1.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"No new external input or credential handling was added. The sealed root comparison is path-normalized; L1 is disclosed under assumption-integrity. N1 is a sealed-worktree integrity gap, not an input-validation or secret-exposure issue.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The two-layer CLI and Store guard is proportionate to the failure cause; a CLI-only flag would leave other Store callers able to publish. It avoids a broader filesystem policy. The choice would be incomplete unless every exported assessment writer, including the markdown writer in N1, is guarded.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone --strict\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable did not return a captured completion status; the checkout was subsequently changed by that older executable, so no pass can be claimed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-design\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The design assessment returned observed with no structural deltas.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-discover\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The closeout check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The review check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Rule selection returned backend-go, security, and documentation-style for pose-mcp.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The attempted installed-CLI check did not return a captured completion status; the stale executable makes the result untrustworthy.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed validation evidence because a fresh strict run could not be safely trusted after the installed CLI changed the checkout.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed module validation evidence; the focused current-source Go tests and vet passed separately.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go\",\n      \"line\": 658,\n      \"summary\": \"GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown writes .pose/assessments/<slug>.md without refuseSealedAssessmentWrite, so a Store caller can still mutate the sealed checkout despite the guards on SaveComponentState and the other assessment writers.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Verified review_dispatch.go appends POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT for the checkout and IsSealedCheckout resolves and compares the paths. L1 remains an accepted limitation: a reviewer process that clears the variable can write, with the dispatch tree comparison detecting the mutation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds no shared mutable state or asynchronous lifecycle. The no-persist paths skip publication; the focused Assess and ReviewPlanRunsAssessments Go tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sealed CLI write commands return a refusal, while Store assessment writes use the typed ErrSealedAssessmentWrite error. Focused CLI and pose package tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays within the pose-mcp assessment CLI and Store boundary; sealed integration evidence covers delegated review checkout handling.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI emits a persistence hint on stderr and direct Store callers receive a typed error with a remediation hint.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The three flags are additive; persisting paths remain the default outside a sealed checkout, JSON output keeps the same result shape, and no stored record schema changes.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"R1/R2 address persisted assessment files as the cause of sealed-run failures; D1'\"'s CLI skip plus Store guard is the smallest direct backstop, and D2 makes planned commands safe when copied. The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there are no delta mappings.\\\",\\\"mappings\\\":[]},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared the English and pt-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies with the CLI behavior and help entries; they describe --no-persist, sealed checkout behavior, refusal commands, and planned flags consistently.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The refusal paths explain why writes are blocked and the Store error names --no-persist. The focused tests passed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Changes are confined to the assessment CLI and Store writers, review plan, help, and the specified manuals/scaffold copies. The one omitted writer guard is recorded as N1.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"No new external input or credential handling was added. The sealed root comparison is path-normalized; L1 is disclosed under assumption-integrity. N1 is a sealed-worktree integrity gap, not an input-validation or secret-exposure issue.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The two-layer CLI and Store guard is proportionate to the failure cause; a CLI-only flag would leave other Store callers able to publish. It avoids a broader filesystem policy. The choice would be incomplete unless every exported assessment writer, including the markdown writer in N1, is guarded.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone --strict\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable did not return a captured completion status; the checkout was subsequently changed by that older executable, so no pass can be claimed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-design\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The design assessment returned observed with no structural deltas.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-discover\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The closeout check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The review check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Rule selection returned backend-go, security, and documentation-style for pose-mcp.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The attempted installed-CLI check did not return a captured completion status; the stale executable makes the result untrustworthy.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed validation evidence because a fresh strict run could not be safely trusted after the installed CLI changed the checkout.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed module validation evidence; the focused current-source Go tests and vet passed separately.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n**Finding N1 — medium, blocker:** [discovery.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:658) exports `GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown`, which creates and writes an assessment file without the sealed-checkout guard. A caller can therefore mutate the sealed checkout directly, bypassing the guards on the other Store writers. This leaves the Store-level guarantee in D1 incomplete.\n\nThe focused Go tests and vet passed: `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'Assess|ReviewPlanRunsAssessments'` and `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose`. The design assessment reported no structural deltas. The final draft preflight **accepted** the conclusion draft below. I did not record an attestation.\n\n**Execution issue:** I ran assessment commands with the installed `pose` executable, which predates the reviewed `--no-persist` change. It printed that it wrote artifacts and changed these tracked files:\n\n- [.pose/assessments/README.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/README.md)\n- [.pose/assessments/consolidated.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/consolidated.md)\n- [.pose/assessments/integrations.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/integrations.md)\n- [.pose/assessments/pose-mcp.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/pose-mcp.md)\n- [.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md)\n- [.pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json)\n- [.pose/state/integrations.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/integrations.json)\n- [.pose/state/technical-debt.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/technical-debt.json)\n\nI left them untouched under the no-edit boundary. The artifact-check and surface-check attempts did not return a captured completion status, so the draft records them as failed; this is a review-run limitation, not an additional subject-code finding.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go\",\n      \"line\": 658,\n      \"summary\": \"GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown writes .pose/assessments/<slug>.md without refuseSealedAssessmentWrite, so a Store caller can still mutate the sealed checkout despite the guards on SaveComponentState and the other assessment writers.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Verified review_dispatch.go appends POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT for the checkout and IsSealedCheckout resolves and compares the paths. L1 remains an accepted limitation: a reviewer process that clears the variable can write, with the dispatch tree comparison detecting the mutation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds no shared mutable state or asynchronous lifecycle. The no-persist paths skip publication; the focused Assess and ReviewPlanRunsAssessments Go tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sealed CLI write commands return a refusal, while Store assessment writes use the typed ErrSealedAssessmentWrite error. Focused CLI and pose package tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays within the pose-mcp assessment CLI and Store boundary; sealed integration evidence covers delegated review checkout handling.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI emits a persistence hint on stderr and direct Store callers receive a typed error with a remediation hint.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The three flags are additive; persisting paths remain the default outside a sealed checkout, JSON output keeps the same result shape, and no stored record schema changes.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"R1/R2 address persisted assessment files as the cause of sealed-run failures; D1's CLI skip plus Store guard is the smallest direct backstop, and D2 makes planned commands safe when copied. The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there are no delta mappings.\",\"mappings\":[]},\n    {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the English and pt-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies with the CLI behavior and help entries; they describe --no-persist, sealed checkout behavior, refusal commands, and planned flags consistently.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The refusal paths explain why writes are blocked and the Store error names --no-persist. The focused tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"Changes are confined to the assessment CLI and Store writers, review plan, help, and the specified manuals/scaffold copies. The one omitted writer guard is recorded as N1.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"No new external input or credential handling was added. The sealed root comparison is path-normalized; L1 is disclosed under assumption-integrity. N1 is a sealed-worktree integrity gap, not an input-validation or secret-exposure issue.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"The two-layer CLI and Store guard is proportionate to the failure cause; a CLI-only flag would leave other Store callers able to publish. It avoids a broader filesystem policy. The choice would be incomplete unless every exported assessment writer, including the markdown writer in N1, is guarded.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone --strict\",\"rationale\":\"The installed pose executable did not return a captured completion status; the checkout was subsequently changed by that older executable, so no pass can be claimed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\",\"rationale\":\"The design assessment returned observed with no structural deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess integrate --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"not-used\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\"rationale\":\"The closeout check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\"rationale\":\"The review check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Rule selection returned backend-go, security, and documentation-style for pose-mcp.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The attempted installed-CLI check did not return a captured completion status; the stale executable makes the result untrustworthy.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\"rationale\":\"Cited the bundle's sealed validation evidence because a fresh strict run could not be safely trusted after the installed CLI changed the checkout.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Cited the bundle's sealed module validation evidence; the focused current-source Go tests and vet passed separately.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
